{"command":"cd /home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport math\ndef v2(n): return (n & -n).bit_length()-1\ndef monier(n, fac):\n    # exact strong-liar count: (1 + (2^{vw}-1)/(2^w-1)) * prod gcd(d, d_p)\n    d = (n-1) >> v2(n-1)\n    ps = list(fac)\n    w = len(ps)\n    nu = min(v2(p-1) for p in ps)\n    dps = [(p-1) >> v2(p-1) for p in ps]\n    L = (1 + (2**(nu*w)-1)//(2**w-1))\n    for dp in dps: L *= math.gcd(d, dp)\n    return L\nfor n, fac in [(4544947489, {32717:1, 138917:1}),\n               (45881945187, {3:1,13:1,53:1,22197361:1})]:\n    L = monier(n, fac)\n    phi4 = 1\n    for p,e in fac.items(): phi4 *= (p-1)*p**(e-1)\n    print(f\"{n}: exact strong liars = {L}  = phi(n)/{phi4//L if L else 0}\"\n          f\"  (fraction {L/n:.2e}; Monier-Rabin max = phi(n)/4)\")\n    print(f\"   ratio to max: {4*L/phi4:.4f}\")\nPY","description":"Exact Monier strong-liar counts"}